0 -13.2 Td(performed at one or more points along the chromosome\), and mutation. A mutation consisted of replacing one)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(symbol in the chromosome with a randomly chosen symbol from the A\226Z and a\226p alphabets. Kitano used)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(what he called "adaptive mutation": the probability of mutation of an offspring depended on the Hamming)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(distance \(number of mismatches\) between the two parents. High distance resulted in low mutation, and vice)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(versa. In this way, the GA tended to respond to loss of diversity in the population by selectively raising the)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(mutation rate.)Tj
0 -26.4 Td(Kitano \(1990\) performed a series of experiments on evolving networks for simple "encoder/decoder")Tj
0 -13.2 Td(problems to compare the grammatical and direct encoding approaches. He found that, on these relatively)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(simple problems, the performance of a GA using the grammatical encoding method consistently surpassed)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(that of a GA using the direct encoding method, both in the correctness of the resulting neural networks and in)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(the speed with which they were found by the GA. An example of Kitano's results is given in figure 2.24,)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(which plots the error rate of the best network in the population \(averaged over 20 runs\) versus generation. In)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(the grammatical encoding runs, the GA found networks with lower error rate, and found the best networks)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(more quickly, than in the direct encoding runs. Kitano also discovered that the performance of the GA scaled)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(much better with network size when grammatical encoding was used\227performance decreased very quickly)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(with network size when direct encoding was used, but stayed much more constant with grammatical encoding.)Tj
0 -26.4 Td(What accounts for the grammatical encoding method's apparent superiority? Kitano argues that the)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(grammatical encoding method can easily create "regular," repeated patterns of connectivity, and that this is a)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(result of the repeated patterns that naturally come from repeatedly applying grammatical rules. We would)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(expect grammatical encoding approaches to perform well on problems requiring this kind of regularity.)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(Grammatical encoding also has the advantage of requiring shorter chromosomes, since the GA works on the)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(instructions for building the network \(the grammar\) rather than on the network structure itself. For complex)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(networks, the latter could be huge and intractable for any search algorithm.)Tj
0 -26.4 Td(Although these attributes might lend an advantage in general to the grammatical encoding method, it is not)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(clear that they accounted for the grammatical encoding method's superiority in the experiments reported by)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(Kitano \(1990\). The encoder/decoder problem is one of the simplest)Tj
