0 -13.2 Td(non-Lamarckian mechanism was)Tj
( made by J.M. Baldwin \(1896\), who pointed out that if learning helps)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(survival then the organisms best able to learn will have the most offspring, thus increasing the frequency of)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(the genes responsible for learning. And if the environment remains relatively fixed, so that the best things to)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(learn remain constant, this can lead, via selection, to a genetic encoding of a trait that originally had to be)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(learned. \(Note that Baldwin's proposal was published long before the detailed mechanisms of genetic)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(inheritance were known.\) For example, an organism that has the capacity to learn that a particular plant is)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(poisonous will be more likely to survive \(by learning not to eat the plant\) than organisms that are unable to)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(learn this information, and thus will be more likely to produce offspring that also have this learning capacity.)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(Evolutionary variation will have a chance to work on this line of offspring, allowing for the possibility that the)Tj
