0 -13.2 Td(maintain, but they do not add much to the survival powers of the organism, and in some cases they can be)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(positively harmful \(e.g., excessively long tail feathers on birds that interfere with flying\). Where did such)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(traits come from, and why do they persist? The answer\227first proposed by Darwin himself\227is most likely)Tj
0 -13.2 Td("sexual selection." Sexual selection occurs when females \(typically\) of a particular species tend to select)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(mates according to some criterion \(e.g., who has the biggest, most elaborate plumage or antlers\), so males)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(having those traits are more likely to be chosen by females as mates. The offspring of such matings tend to)Tj
