/F6 11 Tf ( t)Tj
/F4 11 Tf ( gene\). Females expressed only the)Tj
/F6 11 Tf ( p)Tj
/F4 11 Tf ( gene, males only)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(the)Tj
/F6 11 Tf ( t)Tj
/F4 11 Tf ( gene. Each gene could be either 0 or 1. The population was not infinite, of course, but it was large:)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(131,072 individuals \(equal to twice the number of processors on the Connection Machine 2\). The initial)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(population contained equal numbers of males and females, and there was a particular initial distribution of 0)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(and 1 alleles for)Tj
/F6 11 Tf ( t)Tj
/F4 11 Tf ( and)Tj
/F6 11 Tf ( p)Tj
/F4 11 Tf (. At each generation a certain number of the)Tj
/F6 11 Tf ( t)Tj
/F4 11 Tf ( = 1 males were killed off before)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(reproduction began; each female then chose a surviving male to mate with. In the first simulation, the choice)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(was made by sampling a small number of surviving males throughout the population and deciding which one)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(to mate with probabilistically as a function of the value of the female's)Tj
