/F4 11 Tf 0 687 Td 0.000 Tc(Like many of the other models we have looked at, Echo is meant to be as simple as possible while still)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(capturing essential aspects of ecological systems. It is not meant to model any particular ecosystem \(although)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(more detailed versions might someday be used to do so\); it is meant to)Tj
( capture general properties common to)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(all ecosystems. It is intended to be a platform for controlled experiments that can reveal how changes in the)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(model and in its parameters affect phenomena such as the relative abundance of different species, the)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(development and stability of food webs, conditions for and times to extinction, and the evolution of symbiotic)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(communities of organisms.)Tj
0 -26.4 Td(Echo's world\227a two-dimensional lattice of sites\227contains several different types of "resources," represented)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(in the model by letters of the alphabet. These can be thought of as potential sources of energy for the)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(organisms. Different types of resources appear in varying amounts at different sites.)Tj
0 -26.4 Td(The world is populated by "agents," similar in some ways to the agents in the ERL model. Each agent has a)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(genotype and a phenotype. The genotype encodes a set of rules that govern the types and quantities of)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(resources the agent needs to live and reproduce, the types and quantities of resources the agent can take up)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(from the environment, how the agent will interact with other agents, and some physical characteristics of the)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(agent that are visible to other agents. The phenotype is the agent's resulting behavior and physical appearance)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(\(the latter is represented as a bit pattern\). As in the ERL model, each agent has an internal energy store where)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(it hoards the resources it takes from the environment and from other agents. An agent uses up its stored energy)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(when it moves, when it interacts with other agents, and even when it is simply sitting still \(there is a)Tj
0 -13.2 Td("metabolic tax" for just existing\). An agent can reproduce when it has enough energy stored up to create a)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(copy of its genome. If its energy store goes below a certain threshold, the agent dies, and its remaining)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(resources are returned to the site at which it lived.)Tj
0 -26.4 Td(At each time step, agents living at the same site encounter one another at random. There are three different)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(types of interactions they can have:combat, trade, and mating. \(An Echo wag once remarked that these are the)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(three elements of a good marriage.\) When two agents meet, they decide which type of interaction to have on)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(the basis of their own internal rules and the outward physical appearance of the other agent. If they engage in)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(combat, the outcome is decided by the rules encoded in the genomes of the agents. The loser dies, and all its)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(stored resources are added to the winner's store.)Tj
0 -26.4 Td(If the two agents are less warlike and more commercial, they can agree to trade. An agent's decision to trade is)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(again made on the basis of its internal rules and the other agent's external appearance. Agents trade any stored)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(resources in excess of what they need to reproduce. In Echo an agent has the possibility to evolve)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(deception\227it might look on the outside as though it has something good to trade whereas it actually has)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(nothing. This can result in other agents' getting "fleeced" unless they evolve the capacity \(via internal rules\) to)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(recognize cheaters.)Tj
0 -39.6 Td(Finally, for more amorous agents, mating is a possibility. The decision to mate is, like combat and trade,)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(based on an agent's internal rules and the external appearance of the potential mate. If two agents decide to)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(mate, their chromosomes are combined via two-point crossover to form two offspring, which then replace)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(their parents at the given site. \(After reproducing, the parents die.\))Tj
0 -26.4 Td(If an agent lives through a time step without gaining any resources, it gives up its current site and moves on to)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(another nearby site \(picked at random\), hoping for greener pastures.)Tj
0 -26.4 Td(The three types of interactions are meant to be idealized versions of the basic types of interactions between)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(organisms that occur in nature. They are more extensive than the types of interactions in any of the case)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(studies we have looked at so far. The possibilities for complex interactions, the spatial aspects of the system,)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(and the separation between genotype and phenotype give Echo the potential to capture some very interesting)Tj
/F8 11 Tf 121.235 693 Td(Chapter 3: Genetic Algorithms in Scientific Models)Tj
116.149 -720 Td(79)Tj
