0 -13.2 Td(John Holland's original motivation for developing GAs was to construct a theoretical framework for)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(adaptation as seen in nature, and to apply it to the design of artificial adaptive)Tj
( systems. According to Holland)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(\(1975\), an adaptive system must persistently identify, test, and incorporate structural properties hypothesized)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(to give better performance in some environment. Schemas are meant to be a formalization of such structural)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(properties. In the context of genetics, schemas correspond to constellations of genes that work together to)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(effect some adaptation in an organism; evolution discovers and propagates such constellations. Of course,)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(adaptation is possible only in a world in which there is structure in the environment to be discovered and)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(exploited. Adaptation is impossible in a sufficiently random environment.)Tj
