/F4 11 Tf 0 687 Td 0.000 Tc(strategies community, in which parameters such as mutation rate are encoded as part of the chromosome. Here)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(I will describe Lawrence Davis's approach to self-adaptation of operator rates \(Davis 1989,1991\).)Tj
0 -26.4 Td(Davis assigns to each operator a "fitness" which is a function of how many highly fit individuals that operator)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(has contributed to creating over the last several generations. Operators gain high fitness both for directly)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(creating good individuals and for "setting the stage" for good individuals to be created \(that is, creating the)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(ancestors of good individuals\). Davis tested this method in the context of a steady-state GA. Each operator)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(\(e.g., crossover, mutation\) starts out with the same initial fitness. At each time step a single operator is chosen)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(probabilistically \(on the basis of its current fitness\) to create a new individual, which replaces a low-fitness)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(member of the population. Each individual)Tj
/F6 11 Tf ( i)Tj
/F4 11 Tf ( keeps a record of which operator created it. If)Tj
/F6 11 Tf ( i)Tj
/F4 11 Tf ( has fitness higher)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(than the current best fitness, then)Tj
/F6 11 Tf ( i)Tj
/F4 11 Tf ( receives some credit for the operator that created it, as do)Tj
/F6 11 Tf ( i)Tj
/F4 11 Tf (' parents,)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(grandparents, and so on, back to a prespecified level of ancestor. The fitness of each operator over a given)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(time interval is a function of its previous fitness and the sum of the credits received by all the individuals)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(created by that operator during that time period. \(The frequency with which operator fitnesses are updated is a)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(parameter of the method.\) In principle, the dynamically changing fitnesses of operators should keep up with)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(their actual usefulness at different stages of the search, causing the GA to use them at appropriate rates at)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(different times. As far as I know, this ability for the operator fitnesses to keep up with the actual usefulness of)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(the operators has not been tested directly in any way, though Davis showed that this method improved the)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(performance of a GA on some problems \(including, it turns out, Montana and Davis's project on evolving)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(weights for neural networks\).)Tj
0 -26.4 Td(A big question, then, for any adaptive approach to setting parameters\227 including Davis's\227is this: How well)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(does the rate of adaptation of parameter settings match the rate of adaptation in the GA population? The)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(feedback for setting parameters comes from the population's success or failure on the fitness function, but it)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(might be difficult for this information to travel fast enough for the parameter settings to stay up to date with)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(the population's current state. Very little work has been done on measuring these different rates of adaptation)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(and how well they match in different parameter-adaptation experiments. This seems to me to be the most)Tj
0 -13.2 Td(important research to be done in order to get self-adaptation methods to work well.)Tj
